WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.795 --> 00:00:15.616
Lady Kou ran into the courthouse early the next morning.

2
00:00:17.656 --> 00:00:22.118
With tears in her eyes, she told the judge that she had lied the day before.

3
00:00:22.138 --> 00:00:26.879
"The Tang Monk and his companions are innocent."

4
00:00:26.899 --> 00:00:28.579
[g@Lady Kou sniffed.

5
00:00:29.420 --> 00:00:32.865
"Please release them."@g] [g@The judge nodded.

6
00:00:32.885 --> 00:00:39.889
"I was going to release the prisoners this morning."@g] He explained how the Wandering Spirit had visited him

7
00:00:39.989 --> 00:00:40.790
the night before.

8
00:00:41.810 --> 00:00:43.131
Lady Kou gasped.

9
00:00:43.151 --> 00:00:45.653
[g@"My husband visited me last night!

10
00:00:46.473 --> 00:00:52.037
We must release the prisoners at once."@g] [g@They hurried to the Tang Monk's cell.

11
00:00:55.279 --> 00:01:06.574
A guard swung open the cell door.@g] "I'm glad to be out of there," said Wujing.

12
00:01:08.595 --> 00:01:12.518
[g@"Me too," said Bajie with a yawn.

13
00:01:12.538 --> 00:01:19.763
"The beds were very uncomfortable."@g] Lady Kou bowed to the Tang Monk.

14
00:01:19.783 --> 00:01:22.565
"I framed you for killing my husband," she said.

15
00:01:22.585 --> 00:01:24.566
[g@"Please forgive me.

16
00:01:25.126 --> 00:01:28.989
It was a terrible thing to do."@g] [g@"That's right!"

17
00:01:29.249 --> 00:01:30.150
shouted Wukong.

18
00:01:30.170 --> 00:01:37.478
"It was a really terrible thing to do!"@g] [g@The Tang Monk put his hand on the monkey's shoulder.

19
00:01:37.498 --> 00:01:41.401
"Don't yell, Wukong."@g] [g@He looked at Lady Kou.

20
00:01:41.421 --> 00:01:45.304
"We forgive you.@g] [g@The squire was a kind man.

21
00:01:46.144 --> 00:01:52.509
His death is a terrible tragedy."@g] [g@Wukong rubbed his chin.

22
00:01:52.529 --> 00:01:58.913
"I can probably bring him back to life."@g] Lady Kou and the judge were shocked.

23
00:02:00.054 --> 00:02:01.575
"Can you really do that?"

24
00:02:01.955 --> 00:02:03.984
asked Lady Kou.

25
00:02:04.004 --> 00:02:05.265
[g@The Tang Monk smiled.

26
00:02:05.285 --> 00:02:10.486
"Yes, he can.@g] Wukong brought the king of the Black Rooster Kingdom back to life."

27
00:02:11.487 --> 00:02:12.607
He turned to the monkey.

28
00:02:12.627 --> 00:02:15.408
[g@"The sage Laozi helped you that time.

29
00:02:16.048 --> 00:02:19.629
Will you ask him for help again?"@g] [g@"No," said Wukong.

30
00:02:19.649 --> 00:02:25.071
"Laozi doesn't really like me.@g] I'll go to the Land of Darkness and talk to the Judge of

31
00:02:25.111 --> 00:02:25.971
the Dead instead."

32
00:02:30.624 --> 00:02:34.867
When Wukong entered the Palace of Darkness, the Judge of the Dead frowned.

33
00:02:34.887 --> 00:02:38.169
"Why are you here, Wukong?

34
00:02:39.110 --> 00:02:44.974
You already made yourself immortal by crossing out your name in the Directory."

35
00:02:44.994 --> 00:02:47.195
Wukong laughed.

36
00:02:47.215 --> 00:02:50.297
[g@"I wondered if you would remember that.

37
00:02:51.638 --> 00:02:55.901
I'm looking for Squire Kou's name."@g] "Squire Kou?"

38
00:02:56.882 --> 00:03:00.164
The judge opened the Directory and flipped through some pages.

39
00:03:01.604 --> 00:03:02.565
"Ah, yes.

40
00:03:03.605 --> 00:03:05.567
He died two days ago.

41
00:03:06.767 --> 00:03:10.670
He now works for the bodhisattva Dayuan in the Jade Palace.

42
00:03:11.791 --> 00:03:13.972
It's here in the Land of Darkness."

43
00:03:16.213 --> 00:03:18.134
Wukong went to the Jade Palace.

44
00:03:18.154 --> 00:03:22.877
"Greetings, Sun Wukong," said the bodhisattva.

45
00:03:22.897 --> 00:03:25.779
"Greetings, Bodhisattva."

46
00:03:25.979 --> 00:03:26.920
The monkey bowed.

47
00:03:28.164 --> 00:03:31.766
"Two nights ago a friend of mine, Squire Kou, was killed and brought here.

48
00:03:33.767 --> 00:03:35.207
I would like to bring him back to Earth."

49
00:03:35.227 --> 00:03:38.829
[g@The bodhisattva raised an eyebrow.

50
00:03:39.129 --> 00:03:43.371
"You want him to return to life?"@g] "Yes," said Wukong.

51
00:03:43.391 --> 00:03:48.073
"I'm helping the Tang Monk reach the Western Paradise to fetch the True Scriptures.

52
00:03:49.333 --> 00:03:51.194
The squire was very kind to us."

53
00:03:52.395 --> 00:03:53.896
The bodhisattva smiled.

54
00:03:54.296 --> 00:03:54.816
"Very well.

55
00:03:55.744 --> 00:03:59.126
The squire may return to Earth until it's time for him to come back here."

56
00:04:01.448 --> 00:04:03.990
The bodhisattva brought Wukong to an office.

57
00:04:08.793 --> 00:04:13.936
Squire Kou was sitting behind a large desk, smiling, as he studied some documents.

58
00:04:17.078 --> 00:04:19.180
His eyes sparkled when he saw Wukong.

59
00:04:19.200 --> 00:04:22.262
[g@"It's good to see you, Wukong!"

60
00:04:22.482 --> 00:04:23.262
said the squire.

61
00:04:23.283 --> 00:04:28.301
"What are you doing here?"@g] "I have good news," said the monkey.

62
00:04:28.321 --> 00:04:30.662
[g@"Your life isn't over yet.

63
00:04:31.782 --> 00:04:35.884
I'm taking you back to Earth."@g] [g@The squire looked confused.

64
00:04:36.524 --> 00:04:41.827
He glanced at the bodhisattva.@g] [g@The bodhisattva nodded.

65
00:04:41.847 --> 00:04:48.029
"You may return to Earth.@g] When your life is over, you will return to your job here."

66
00:04:49.370 --> 00:04:52.251
The squire came out from behind his desk and bowed.

67
00:04:52.271 --> 00:04:54.172
"Thank you, Bodhisattva.

68
00:04:55.524 --> 00:04:58.810
I am happy here, but I would love to see my wife and friends again."

69
00:04:58.830 --> 00:05:02.156
[g@Wukong moved closer to the squire.

70
00:05:02.176 --> 00:05:08.967
"You'll be home soon, Squire."@g] The monkey recited a spell, and the squire vanished.
